 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission includes a base revision ID, the system SHALL accept it only if that revision is the latest resolved revision for the visit at submission time.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When the first submission for a visit is accepted, the system SHALL create a revision with status resolved, base revision ID null, and the submitted payload.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a subsequent submission with a valid base revision ID is accepted and no competing revisions exist for that base, the system SHALL create a revision with status resolved whose base revision ID is the previous resolved revision.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a subsequent submission with a valid base revision ID is accepted and competing revisions already exist for that base, the system SHALL create a revision with status competing and record it in the same revision cycle.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a submission's base revision ID does not match the latest resolved revision for the visit, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator resolves a revision cycle, the system SHALL create a new revision with status resolved, base revision ID pointing to the latest resolved revision, and the resolved payload provided by the coordinator.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a revision cycle is resolved, the system SHALL mark all competing revisions in that cycle as superseded.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a revision cycle is resolved, the system SHALL record the resolving coordinator's ID, the resolution timestamp, and the set of resolved revision IDs.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: When retrieving the current visit, the system SHALL return the latest resolved revision payload if one exists, or 404 if no resolved revision exists.
+- [ ] **REC-016**: When retrieving the current visit and an unresolved revision cycle exists, the system SHALL include a flag indicating unresolved work is present.
+- [ ] **REC-017**: When retrieving visit history, the system SHALL return all revisions for the visit ordered by server receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-018**: When querying open review cycles, the system SHALL return all cycles containing competing revisions that have not been resolved.
+- [ ] **REC-019**: When a visit has no resolved revision and an open revision cycle exists, the system SHALL indicate the visit has no current state.
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When validating a submission, the system SHALL verify the visit ID refers to a valid catalog plot, field types are correct, and the observer list is non-empty.
